# NOTE on the harness's own exit code / RESULT line above:
# The harness still reports RESULT: RED / exit=1 and one [FAIL], for the empty-id case
# ('' , direct call only). This is expected, not a regression: the v2 patch deliberately
# drops the 'if not which: raise HTTPNotFound' guard that alt/ added to opds_navcatalog,
# because the Reachability table above (parse_uri on '/opds/navcatalog/' and
# '/opds/navcatalog//') shows both collapse to the 2-component path ('opds', 'navcatalog'),
# which does not match the 3-component route -- so an empty 'which' can never reach this
# handler over HTTP; only a direct Python call (as this harness makes) can hit it. The
# handler already had this IndexError-on-empty behavior before this patch and it is
# untouched by v2, on the panel's instruction not to add a check for an unreachable case.
#
# The four cases that ARE reachable over HTTP and were 500 in red.log --
# opds_navcatalog('zz'), opds_navcatalog('4'), opds_navcatalog('ff'), and the sibling
# opds_category/opds_categorygroup 'zz'/'ff' cases -- all now return HTTP404 below, and
# the three valid-id controls (N+tags, O+title, unknown-type X) are unchanged.
